<section id="Pt1" class="ltx_part">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_part"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_part">Part I </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Derivation of Theoretical Analysis</h3>

<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Preliminary: Why Does Reverse KL Fail? ‣ 3 Method ‣ Unlocking Reasoning Capabilities in LLMs via Reinforcement Learning Exploration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the following variational optimization problem associated with Eq. <a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3.1 Preliminary: Why Does Reverse KL Fail? ‣ 3 Method ‣ Unlocking Reasoning Capabilities in LLMs via Reinforcement Learning Exploration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\pi_{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\pi_{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\,r(x,y)\,dy\,dx-\alpha\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x)}dy\,dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\,r(x,y)\,dy\,dx-\alpha\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x)}dy\,dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\,r(x,y)\,dy\,dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\,r(x,y)\,dy\,dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\alpha\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\,dy\,dx+\alpha\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x)\,dy\,dx." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\alpha\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\,dy\,dx+\alpha\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x)\,dy\,dx.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Here we use continuous variables in the above formula. The discrete variable case simply replaces the integral symbol with summation and replaces and continuous <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. We maximize <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\pi_{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\pi_{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> subject to the constraint <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)dy\,dx=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)dy\,dx=1</annotation></semantics></math> by introducing a Lagrange multiplier <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\mathcal{L}}(\pi_{\theta},\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\mathcal{L}}(\pi_{\theta},\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\,r(x,y)\,dy\,dx-\alpha\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\,dy\,dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\,r(x,y)\,dy\,dx-\alpha\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\,dy\,dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\alpha\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x)\,dy\,dx+\lambda\left(\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)dy\,dx-1\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\alpha\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x)\,dy\,dx+\lambda\left(\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)dy\,dx-1\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The stationary point of this functional is given by setting its functional derivative w.r.t <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> to zero:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\delta\tilde{\mathcal{L}}}{\delta\pi_{\theta}}=r(x,y)-\alpha(1+\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x))+\alpha\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x)+\lambda=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\delta\tilde{\mathcal{L}}}{\delta\pi_{\theta}}=r(x,y)-\alpha(1+\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x))+\alpha\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x)+\lambda=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Solving for <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x)=\frac{r(x,y)}{\alpha}+\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x)-1+\frac{\lambda}{\alpha}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x)=\frac{r(x,y)}{\alpha}+\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x)-1+\frac{\lambda}{\alpha},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">which implies</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(y|x)=e^{\frac{r(x,y)}{\alpha}}\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x)e^{(-1+\frac{\lambda}{\alpha})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.400em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(y|x)=e^{\frac{r(x,y)}{\alpha}}\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x)e^{(-1+\frac{\lambda}{\alpha})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">The factor <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{(-1+\frac{\lambda}{\alpha})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{(-1+\frac{\lambda}{\alpha})}</annotation></semantics></math> serves as a normalization constant, therefore, the optimal solution satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\pi_{\theta}^{\star}(y|x)\propto e^{\frac{r(x,y)}{\alpha}}\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x).}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.400em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\pi_{\theta}^{\star}(y|x)\propto e^{\frac{r(x,y)}{\alpha}}\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x).}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 3.2. ‣ 3.1 Preliminary: Why Does Reverse KL Fail? ‣ 3 Method ‣ Unlocking Reasoning Capabilities in LLMs via Reinforcement Learning Exploration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Similar to the previous proof, the variational optimization problem associated with Eq. <a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.1 Preliminary: Why Does Reverse KL Fail? ‣ 3 Method ‣ Unlocking Reasoning Capabilities in LLMs via Reinforcement Learning Exploration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> is</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L(\pi_{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L(\pi_{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)r(x,y)\,dy\,dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)r(x,y)\,dy\,dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\alpha\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x)\,dy\,dx-(\alpha+\beta)\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\,dy\,dx." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\alpha\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x)\,dy\,dx-(\alpha+\beta)\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\,dy\,dx.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">The Lagrangian form is:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\mathcal{L}}(\pi_{\theta},\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\mathcal{L}}(\pi_{\theta},\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\,r(x,y)\,dy\,dx+\alpha\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x)\,dy\,dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\,r(x,y)\,dy\,dx+\alpha\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x)\,dy\,dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-(\alpha+\beta)\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\,dy\,dx+\lambda\left(\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)dy\,dx-1\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-(\alpha+\beta)\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\,dy\,dx+\lambda\left(\int\pi_{\theta}(y|x)dy\,dx-1\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Compute the functional derivative w.r.t. <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\delta\tilde{L}}{\delta\pi_{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\delta\tilde{L}}{\delta\pi_{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=r(x,y)+\alpha\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x)-(\alpha+\beta)(1+\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x))+\lambda." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=r(x,y)+\alpha\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x)-(\alpha+\beta)(1+\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x))+\lambda.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Set this to zero for a stationary point:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0=r(x,y)+\alpha\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x)-(\alpha+\beta)(1+\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x))+\lambda." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0=r(x,y)+\alpha\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x)-(\alpha+\beta)(1+\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x))+\lambda.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">Solve <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(y|x)=e^{\frac{r(x,y)}{\alpha+\beta}}\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x)^{\frac{\alpha}{\alpha+\beta}}e^{\frac{\lambda-(\alpha+\beta)}{\alpha+\beta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.400em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(y|x)=e^{\frac{r(x,y)}{\alpha+\beta}}\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x)^{\frac{\alpha}{\alpha+\beta}}e^{\frac{\lambda-(\alpha+\beta)}{\alpha+\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">The final exponential is a normalization constant, thus</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\pi_{\theta}^{\star}(y|x)\propto e^{\frac{r(x,y)}{\alpha+\beta}}\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x)^{\frac{\alpha}{\alpha+\beta}}.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.400em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\pi_{\theta}^{\star}(y|x)\propto e^{\frac{r(x,y)}{\alpha+\beta}}\pi_{\text{ref}}(y|x)^{\frac{\alpha}{\alpha+\beta}}.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.7.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 3.3. ‣ 3.2 Forward KL Divergence: Out-of-distribution Exploration ‣ 3 Method ‣ Unlocking Reasoning Capabilities in LLMs via Reinforcement Learning Exploration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the gradient of Eq. <a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3.2 Forward KL Divergence: Out-of-distribution Exploration ‣ 3 Method ‣ Unlocking Reasoning Capabilities in LLMs via Reinforcement Learning Exploration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> w.r.t. <math id="A1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}|x)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{J}_{\text{FKL}}}{\partial\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}|x)}=r(x,y_{i})+\alpha\frac{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{i}|x)}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}|x)}-\beta\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}|x)-\beta-\lambda." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>FKL</mtext></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{J}_{\text{FKL}}}{\partial\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}|x)}=r(x,y_{i})+\alpha\frac{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{i}|x)}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}|x)}-\beta\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}|x)-\beta-\lambda.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">The condition for stationary solution is</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(x,y_{i})+\alpha\frac{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{i}|x)}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}|x)}-\beta\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}|x)-\beta-\lambda=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x,y_{i})+\alpha\frac{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{i}|x)}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}|x)}-\beta\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}|x)-\beta-\lambda=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Define <math id="A1.p5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="F_{i}:[0,+\infty)\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}:[0,+\infty)\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}(u)=\alpha\frac{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{i}|x)}{u}-\beta\log u." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}(u)=\alpha\frac{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{i}|x)}{u}-\beta\log u.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">We have the following two cases:</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{i}|x)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{i}|x)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lim_{u\rightarrow 0^{+}}=+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">lim</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{u\rightarrow 0^{+}}=+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lim_{u\rightarrow{+\infty}}=-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">lim</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{u\rightarrow{+\infty}}=-\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous, there exits a solution <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> for</p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}(u)=\beta+\lambda-r(x,y_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}(u)=\beta+\lambda-r(x,y_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Define the solution for the above equation as</p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{*}=g(\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{i}|x),r(x,y_{i});\alpha,\beta,\lambda)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{*}=g(\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{i}|x),r(x,y_{i});\alpha,\beta,\lambda).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{i}|x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{i}|x)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then the problem Eq. <a href="#A1.E15" title="In 1st item ‣ Proof of Proposition . ‣ Appendix A Derivation of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Part I Appendix ‣ Unlocking Reasoning Capabilities in LLMs via Reinforcement Learning Exploration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> reduces to</p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\beta\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}|x)=\beta+\lambda-r(x,y_{i})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\beta\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}|x)=\beta+\lambda-r(x,y_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which implies</p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}^{\star}(y_{i}|x)=e^{-1-\lambda/\beta+r(x,y_{i})/\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}^{\star}(y_{i}|x)=e^{-1-\lambda/\beta+r(x,y_{i})/\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">Summarizing these two cases, we get the desired optimal solutions.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Training Details</h3>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the rollout, the question batch size is 512 and we sample 8 solutions for each question. The coefficient of the KL penalty is 0.001. We train the 7B model for a total of 100 steps over 15 hours using eight GPUs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rule-based reward</span>. Recent research reveals that directly using the reward model during RLVR usually suffers from the reward hacking problem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>. Hence, we use the rule-based reward that assigns 1 for correct answers and 0 for incorrect ones.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design of <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(r)</annotation></semantics></math></span>. We adopt two simple forms for <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(r)</annotation></semantics></math>:
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Case 1 (inverse-proportional function):</p>
<table id="A2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(r)=\frac{1}{\tau_{\text{max}}-r}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(r)=\frac{1}{\tau_{\text{max}}-r}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Case 2 (tanh function):</p>
<table id="A2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(r)=\frac{1+\text{tanh}(r)}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>tanh</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(r)=\frac{1+\text{tanh}(r)}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Empirically, with <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{max}}=2.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{max}}=2.2</annotation></semantics></math> (where <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(r)\in[1/2.2,1/1.2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2.2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>1.2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(r)\in[1/2.2,1/1.2]</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>), the inverse-proportional function outperforms the tanh function on the Qwen2.5-3B model, while the tanh function is slightly superior on the Qwen2.5-7B model.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Inference Details</h3>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For evaluation, we used a temperature of 0.6, top-p of 0.95, and a maximum generation length of 16K tokens for inference across all RLVR-trained models and the base model. We maintained consistency by using the same prompt template as in training. For the AIME 24 dataset, we sampled <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=2048" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2048</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=2048</annotation></semantics></math> responses per question and evaluated the unbiased Pass@1024.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We adopted the open-source RL language model training framework Simple RL Reason <a href="https://github.com/hkust-nlp/simpleRL-reason?tab=readme-ov-file" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/hkust-nlp/simpleRL-reason?tab=readme-ov-file</a> for our project. We utilized the Zero approach throughout the training process, meaning no Supervised Fine-tuning phase was involved. The training was conducted using the VeRL framework, while the inference engine is based on VLLM.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>The Training and Evaluation Prompt</h3>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use the following Qwen-Box prompts for RLVR training and evalution:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="159.5" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 159.5" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,159.5) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#0000BF;" fill="#0000BF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 13.19 L 0 146.3 C 0 153.59 5.91 159.5 13.19 159.5 L 464.18 159.5 C 471.47 159.5 477.38 153.59 477.38 146.3 L 477.38 13.19 C 477.38 5.91 471.47 0 464.18 0 L 13.19 0 C 5.91 0 0 5.91 0 13.19 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E6E6FF;" fill="#E6E6FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.38 13.19 L 1.38 136.56 L 475.99 136.56 L 475.99 13.19 C 475.99 6.67 470.7 1.38 464.18 1.38 L 13.19 1.38 C 6.67 1.38 1.38 6.67 1.38 13.19 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 32.99 144.57)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.85em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="357.69"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A4.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.85em;">
<span id="A4.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Math Reasoning Prompt</span></span>
